 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Cameroon has 10 regions and 58 divisions. Each has a headquarters (chief town) where the governor or the senior divisional officer works.\nRegional headquarters: Adamawa – Ngaoundéré; Centre – Yaoundé; East – Bertoua; Far North – Maroua; Littoral – Douala; North – Garoua; North West – Bamenda; South – Ebolowa; South West – Buea; West – Bafoussam.\nExamples of divisions and headquarters: Fako – Limbe; Meme – Kumba; Mezam – Bamenda; Bui – Kumbo; Wouri – Douala; Mfoundi – Yaoundé; Mifi – Bafoussam; Benoue – Garoua; Diamaré – Maroua; Océan – Kribi.\nMethod: on a blank map of Cameroon, draw the regional boundaries, mark each headquarters with a dot and its name, add a title, a key and a north arrow.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "X": {
    "pick": [
     {
      "r": "South West",
      "c": "Buea"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "problem": "What is the headquarters of the {X.r} Region?",
  "steps": [
   "Look up the {X.r} in the list of regions.",
   "Its headquarters is {X.c}."
  ],
  "answer": "{X.c}",
  "checks": []
 },
